### keywords

- authfn/core, services/account/src/auth.ts, social-oauth.ts, oauth-support.ts, package barrel, source provenance, Just answer, superfunctions-dev/authfn/core

## Task 2: Clarify exactly what source was read and where it lives, success

### rollout_summary_files


### keywords

- did you read actual source code, where is the source code, services/account/node_modules/@authfn/core, file:../../../superfunctions-dev/authfn/core, symlink target, epistemic honesty

## User preferences

- when the user says "Just answer" on repo-opinion prompts -> give a direct judgment first instead of a long design-process preamble. [Task 1]
- when the user asks "Did you read the full source code of authfn/core?" or "do you know where the source code is?" -> answer provenance questions explicitly and distinguish inspected files from the full source tree. [Task 1][Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- `services/account/src/auth.ts` is the composition root for Account auth wiring; it is the right first file when judging how much `@authfn/core` bleeds into app runtime concerns. [Task 1]
- In this workspace, `services/account/node_modules/@authfn/core` resolves to the linked local checkout `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/authfn/core`, so package reads can and should be source-based. [Task 2]
- The current `@authfn/core` surface is broad: its barrel exports app/server creation, auth primitives, HTTP helpers, plugin factories, and OAuth helpers together. [Task 1]
- `src/plugins/social-oauth.ts` is the strongest concrete boundary smell because it mixes OAuth route orchestration, provider handling, account linking, 2FA handoff, session issuance, storage interaction, and diagnostics in one area. [Task 1]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: an architecture opinion sounds stronger than the actual inspection performed. Cause: barrel/public-surface reads are presented as if the whole source tree was audited. Fix: say exactly which files were read and whether the answer is a representative judgment or a full audit. [Task 1][Task 2]
- Symptom: the provenance answer starts with explanation instead of yes/no clarity. Cause: the direct question is answered too late. Fix: lead with whether the read came from actual local source and then add scope boundaries. [Task 2]

