AGENTS.md:10:Agents MUST reuse existing primitives, shared compositions, stores, and utilities when delivering changes. `client/elements` is the permanent portable primitive layer; `client/components` is the permanent portable layer for domain-neutral compositions intended for reuse across capabilities or products, including charts, maps, nested lists, search controls, and time controls. Neither layer may depend directly or transitively on application state, runtime infrastructure, layout, products, features, DataFn, persistence, schema, or domain stores. Product-connected behavior MUST enter through props or narrow host contracts configured by an application, layout, or feature owner. Prefer these layers, helpers such as `generateResourceId` and `generateSimpleRandomId`, and correctly owned logic instead of duplicating behavior. Rationale: reuse stays portable only when reusable presentation is independent of Nucleum composition and state.
AGENTS.md:46:- Preserve the permanent UI dependency direction: `client/components` may compose `client/elements`; `client/elements` MUST NOT depend on `client/components`; both may use generic `client/actions`. Keep application, runtime, layout, product, feature, DataFn, persistence, schema, and store imports out of all three portable UI workspaces, including through transitive utility imports.
AGENTS.md:172:- Established `client/elements`, `client/components`, and `client/actions` as the permanent portable UI foundation, with components retained for credible future shared use regardless of current consumer count.
