docs/architecture/client-boundaries.md:28:`client/elements` is the permanent portable primitive layer. It owns fundamental controls, UI-only types, portable environment state, and narrow host contracts. `client/components` is the permanent portable composition layer. It owns domain-neutral compositions intended for present or future reuse, including charts, maps, nested lists, search controls, file presentation, keyboard listeners, duration inputs, and time selectors. A single current consumer does not make a component feature-owned. `client/application` owns account/settings, library/resource rendering, modal orchestration, command UI, and app-specific integrations. Markdown editing and tags belong to memory; combinations belong to spaces. Shared preferences live in `client/stores/preferences`, and cross-layer billing contracts live in `schema/account`. Keyboard and interaction-mode contracts live in `client/elements/keyboard`; panel and error presentation contracts live in their domain owners. See [type ownership](type-ownership.md) for the complete inventory.
docs/architecture/client-boundaries.md:43:## Current architecture contract
docs/architecture/client-boundaries.md:59:Reactive account session state lives with the account runtime in `client/runtime/account/account.store.ts`. Authentication persistence, bootstrap, sign-in, sign-out, navigation, and DataFn teardown are coordinated by `client/application/account/account-session.ts`. Deletion confirmation and cleanup orchestration live in `client/application/account/account-deletion.ts`; subscription operations live in `client/application/subscription/subscription.ts`; file conversion, thumbnail generation, signing, and local/remote storage live in `client/stores/files/file-upload.ts`. Legacy OAuth initiation belongs to application account composition.

